File Index

/AccessPage.tsx
Purpose: Access tab (Phase 9) — builder token entry (stored in localStorage) with a live status probe (open/none/invalid/API key/master via GET /api/auth/keys), and the master-only API-key panel: create/rotate/revoke behind confirms, show-once issued-token box, master rotation that swaps the stored token automatically; Phase 10 adds a master-only Audit log table (newest first, refresh). Phase 4 (centralized auth): no code change — the token field is source-agnostic, so a key minted via auth-client (service "mud-builder-server") lands in the same 'key' status bucket; only the 'none' status copy was updated to mention that option. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): its hand-rolled toast JSX replaced by the shared features/shared/Toast.js component (own toast state unchanged). Step 6 (error-message audit): found and fixed a real inconsistency in the run(what, action) helper — its SUCCESS toast already said `${what} — done` but its FAILURE toast just dumped the raw exception with no mention of what action failed; now `${what} failed: <message>`. probe()'s outer catch (the initial capabilities load) similarly gained a "server unreachable: " prefix. Phase G: saveToken()/forgetToken() call accountActor.ts's invalidateAccountActorCache() — the only place in this app that changes the stored token, so the only place that needs to bust that cache.

/accountActor.ts
Purpose: Phase G — useIsAccountActor() hook + invalidateAccountActorCache(), backing SaveAsSnippetButton's visibility (a snippet needs an accountId to be owned by; master/local-key/anonymous have none). Module-level-cached GET /api/roles/me: the Areas dashboard can render many Mob/ObjectEditor accordion instances simultaneously, each embedding a SaveAsSnippetButton, so this fires ONE network call regardless of instance count rather than one per mounted editor.

/AccessPage.test.tsx
Purpose: Access tab tests: token prompt→master unlock, API-key status without management, rejected-token flag, create with show-once token, rotate/revoke behind confirms, master-only audit table (and its absence for API keys).
